Looking at this problem, I need to count squares of two types in a 0-1 matrix:
1. Axis-aligned squares (sides parallel to matrix edges)
2. Diagonal squares (sides parallel to diagonals - forming X/diamond shapes)

Each square must:
- Be a solid frame with linewidth 1
- Be at least 2×2
- Contain at least one 1 (the border itself satisfies this)
- Not touch any "foreign" 1 (by side or corner) - meaning no 1s can be adjacent to the border

